# Migration Refresh 5 — Southern Dark Quadrant + Mini-Fix 5

## What this refresh delivers

Eight new entity notes covering the southern dark quadrant, plus two corrections (Mini-Fix 5) carried forward from Refresh 4b's flagged items. All files are working canon migrations from the world vault's `prompts/world_vault/hollow_crown/surface/southern_dark_quadrant/` directory, plus framing corrections to two existing user-vault files derived from the canonical `groups/elder_roots.md` notes.

### New entity notes (in `10_world/geography/hollow-crown/regions/southern-dark-quadrant/`)

- **Southern Dark Quadrant.md** — `type: location`. Region root. Frames the quadrant's structure: layered threshold geography (the corrupted interiors at the [[Rift of Discord]] and [[Shadowed Hollows]], the perimeter corridors that absorb their effects, the controlled access route up to [[Platinum Oath Monastery]]). Civic presence is two institutions: the [[Vigil]] operating from the Monastery, and [[Greymantle]] under the Warden's reputational authority.

- **Rift of Discord.md** — `type: location`. The realm's deepest wound, [[The Platinum Warden|Vindrael]]'s sacrifice site. Holds the ruined **[[Dark Hold]]** as an internal feature (rebel keep, never elevated to its own entity per canon — the Hold is feature, not place). The pit at the Hold's center is where the rebels' channeling shaft collapsed during the Warden's sacrifice; **its depth is unmeasured beyond ~200 paces**. Active corruption with cumulative exposure tiers; elite [[Wardens|Warden]] training ground.

- **Rift of Discord Edge.md** — `type: location`. Perimeter buffer corridor. [[Vigil]]-patrolled. Two-member patrol teams complete a full circuit in approximately two days. Attenuated versions of the Rift's exposure tiers.

- **Platinum Oath Monastery.md** — `type: location`. The [[Vigil]]'s seat. Officially a Rift monitoring station; actually the surviving [[Platinum Accord]]. **[[The Platinum Warden|Vindrael]]'s tomb is in the deepest interior chamber.** Elite [[Wardens|Warden]] training arc culminates here. **Serevane** is the current Vigil leader — vulkar, knew the Platinum Warden personally.

- **Platinum Oath Approach.md** — `type: location`. Fortified mountain corridor up to the Monastery. Three stages (Lower Approach, Middle Ascent, Upper Approach) plus two manned gatehouses. Walled, watched, patrolled. **The journey itself is the filter.**

- **Greymantle.md** — `type: location`. The realm's outlaw edge-settlement. Founded by a [[Discordant War]] veteran. Refuge for those the realm's standard institutions cannot accommodate. Self-governing under the **[[The Warden of Greymantle|Warden of Greymantle]]** — title is descriptive, not institutional. Working trade relationship with the Monastery, professional and circumscribed.

- **Shadowed Hollows.md** (in `shadowed-hollows/` subfolder) — `type: location`. Surface manifestation of the buried [[Temple of Mordrax]]. Diffuse psychological corruption (vs. the Rift's acute physical-adjacent). Cult attractor; [[Sapphire Sentinels]] monitor covertly; [[Wardens]] respond when activity warrants.

- **Shadowed Hollows Approach.md** (in `shadowed-hollows/` subfolder) — `type: location`. Perimeter corridor to the Hollows. Less visible institutional infrastructure than the [[Rift of Discord Edge|Rift Edge]]. The [[Vigil]]'s patrol practice here involves **"attending back"** — maintaining attentive presence without yielding to the Hollows' attentive presence.

### Mini-Fix 5 corrections

- **Heartwood.md** — Elder Druid description expanded to acknowledge **head-of-all-druids** role beyond Heartwood-specific stewardship. Per canonical [[Elder Roots]] groups file: "the Elder Druid of the Heartwood is the head druid of the entire Feywood — the practitioner whose authority runs across the broader community and whose specific stewardship attaches to the Heartwood itself." Also: status changed from `locked` to `working` per project framing (lore is current canon, work-in-progress).

- **Reading Glade.md** — "Study spaces" section pivoted from specific-questions research framing to **land-reading practice**. Per canonical Elder Roots authoring notes: "Reading Glade canon: land-reading practice. The community's site for interpretive work on Feywood signals — observation circles for learning the practice, sustained spaces for individual long-form work, oral-tradition seats for knowledge transmission. NOT primarily a documentary or library institution." Observation circles and oral-tradition seats sections preserved; only the third section reframed.

