## Out of scope flags

### Temple of Mordrax — deferred

The southern dark quadrant's **subterranean source** is the [[Temple of Mordrax]]. Per geography.md, the Temple sits "under Hollows/Rift" at U16-V17, sealed since the founding age and reinforced after the [[Discordant War]]. It does not appear to be in `prompts/world_vault/hollow_crown/surface/southern_dark_quadrant/` — it's not a surface location. **Probable canonical home is somewhere in a subterranean or crystal-caverns folder** I have not yet found in the world vault. The Temple's wikilinks are placed in this refresh as forward references; the entity note itself is deferred until the source is located.

### The Vigil + Platinum Accord faction note — deferred

The [[Vigil]] (operating identity) and [[Platinum Accord]] (historical parent) are referenced extensively across this refresh's notes. Both deserve their own faction entity notes following the Refresh 4b pattern (faction notes in `10_world/factions/`). Inline description in the Monastery and Approach notes covers operational character; a dedicated faction note would carry doctrine, structure, leadership succession, and the [[Sapphire Sentinels]] / [[Wardens]] coordination relationships. **Recommended for a future refresh** — most likely paired with realm-side factions migration.

### The Warden of Greymantle NPC note — deferred

The [[The Warden of Greymantle|Warden]] is described inline in `Greymantle.md`. A dedicated NPC note in `10_world/npcs/` would carry his [[Discordant War]] history, governing approach, relationship with the [[Vigil]], etc. **Per canon, he is not named by personal name** — his identity is title and history. Deferred to a future NPC refresh.

### Serevane NPC note — deferred

Same pattern. [[Serevane]] is the current [[Vigil]] leader, vulkar, knew [[The Platinum Warden]] personally. Inline description in `Platinum Oath Monastery.md` covers her current role and the prophecy she prepares for. Dedicated NPC note deferred.

